WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
How can one little column change an answer by thousands?

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:07.641 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Today we are using written addition and subtraction.

00:00:07.861 --> 00:00:14.080 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
We will line up equal place values and see how regrouping
changes the grouping without changing the amount.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:17.112 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
What happens when a column contains zero?

00:00:17.762 --> 00:00:22.937 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Our learning goal is to add and subtract whole numbers
accurately using written methods.

00:00:23.587 --> 00:00:25.346 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Success criteria.

00:00:25.566 --> 00:00:27.991 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
I can line up matching place values.

00:00:28.211 --> 00:00:30.661 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
I can regroup without changing the total.

00:00:30.881 --> 00:00:33.559 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
I can check subtraction by adding back.

00:00:34.209 --> 00:00:37.272 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Keep ones under ones and tens under tens.

00:00:37.492 --> 00:00:42.394 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Ten units in any column can be exchanged for one unit in the
column to its left.

00:00:42.614 --> 00:00:47.218 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
In subtraction we can exchange one larger unit for ten
smaller units.

00:00:47.868 --> 00:00:53.197 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Add two thousand seven hundred and eighty-six and one
thousand four hundred and fifty-seven.

00:00:53.417 --> 00:00:58.820 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Start at the ones: six plus seven makes thirteen, so
exchange ten ones for one ten.

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:03.991 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Eight tens plus five tens plus the exchanged ten makes
fourteen tens.

00:01:04.211 --> 00:01:06.009 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Continue the regrouping.

00:01:06.229 --> 00:01:10.464 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Seven hundreds plus four hundreds plus one hundred makes
twelve hundreds.

00:01:10.684 --> 00:01:14.464 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
The final total is four thousand two hundred and
forty-three.

00:01:15.114 --> 00:01:20.569 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Now subtract twenty-seven thousand six hundred and
eighty-four from fifty-two thousand.

00:01:20.789 --> 00:01:27.289 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Across the zeros, exchange one thousand for ten hundreds,
then exchange one hundred and one ten as needed.

00:01:27.939 --> 00:01:34.939 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Subtract each place after regrouping: six ones, one ten,
three hundreds, four thousands and two ten-thousands.

00:01:35.159 --> 00:01:38.785 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
The difference is twenty-four thousand three hundred and
sixteen.

00:01:39.005 --> 00:01:40.599 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Add it back to check.

00:01:41.249 --> 00:01:44.085 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Regrouping does not create extra value.

00:01:44.305 --> 00:01:49.134 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
When a zero is involved, exchange from a larger place and
adjust that place too.

00:01:49.354 --> 00:01:52.953 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Our regrouped parts must still add to fifty-two thousand.

00:01:53.173 --> 00:01:56.255 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Checking the total keeps every exchange honest.

00:01:56.905 --> 00:02:00.847 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
What is four hundred and six minus one hundred and
seventy-eight?

00:02:04.847 --> 00:02:06.789 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Regroup across the zero.

00:02:07.009 --> 00:02:13.332 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Sixteen ones minus eight is eight, nine tens minus seven is
two, and three hundreds minus one is two.

00:02:13.552 --> 00:02:16.374 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
The answer is two hundred and twenty-eight.

00:02:17.024 --> 00:02:21.714 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Align place values, regroup without changing the total, and
work systematically.

00:02:21.934 --> 00:02:26.321 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
A zero is a placeholder, so exchanges may cross more than
one column.

00:02:26.541 --> 00:02:28.949 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Use addition to check subtraction.

00:02:29.169 --> 00:02:32.327 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Now choose a strategy and explain why it works.

00:02:32.547 --> 00:02:35.695 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Have a go at the lesson practice on MathMagic!
